[Applause]  lifeguards are in high demand this  summer across the valley jeremy j ford  shows us where they are seeking out  employment  pools across clark county are currently  experiencing a lifeguard shortage but  it's water parks like this with  lifeguards like these that are staffed  up and manning the waters  with temperatures rising each week more  people are flocking to water parks even  pools on the strip  this is causing community pools to limit  its operation hours due to lack of staff  brent anderson is the water safety lead  at cowabunga canyon she says lifeguards  are working at other facilities instead  of community pools due to a more fun and  family-friendly atmosphere they do have  a very important job and they do have to  take a lot of responsibility in the job  but at a workplace like this we do make  it family oriented and we are there for  our lifeguards obviously we're  happy to have more lifeguards here and  welcome more people to the family but  we're just waiting for the moments to  work  currently water parks and hotels are  offering more benefits than community  pools to its seasonal employees this  including advancement higher pay and  paid lifeguard training  in las vegas jeremy j ford live local  down  anyone interested becoming a lifeguard  must be at least 15 years of age able to  pass lifeguard certification first aid  and cpr courses and in some cases like  the city of henderson you have to be at  least 16.

